  "strategy": "Final optimization refinement:\nImplementation-specific optimizations:\n- Lazy convolution computation for adjacent patches\n- Gradient caching with shrinking buffers\n- Piecewise constant sensitivity predictors\n- Adaptive step size: \u03b4 = \u221a(\u03b5) * (1/n) * 2^(generation)\n\nAdvanced configuration:\n- Awakening depth: set to 5 for enhanced robustness\n- Sensitivity buffer size: 3 cosmetically higher than LR-predicted\n- History: Track 10^5 optimization steps for auto-recovery\n\nDetailed interaction protocol:\nCandidate generation:\n1. Start with fixed-length parent\n2. Apply L2 regularization \u03b2=10\u207b\u00b3 in initial steps\n3. Switch to Huber loss (\u03b2=0.1) later stages\n\nBatch processing:\n- Use block optimizations: Process disjoint blocks of size floor(n/5) in parallel\n- Dynamic block splitting based on smoothness detection\n- Atomic writes ensured with compensated weighting\n\nTermination handlers:\n- HEFTI: Hyperbolic exponential failure time handler injects restart upon exponential decay fitting\n- ASPOH: Adaptive step path optimization handler adjusts step size based on peak shape evolution\n- SPICE: Sensitivity pivot insertion checks inserts key elements based on gradient landscape changes\n\nMonitoring schema:\nTrack:\n1. Per-element change rate\n2. Global autocorrelation distribution skewness\n3. First/last peak ratios\n4. Normalization consistency\n\nFallback paths:\n1. Primary: Reversion to initial configuration (helped for difficult modes)\n2. Secondary: Bridge mode between current/fallback configurations (useful for boundaries)\n3. Ultimate: Initialize from parent sequence after parameter reset",
